
==============================================================================
G4-1 matched capacity, different state spaces
==============================================================================
  system                                 N    K   Hilbert d
  regular 3-gon GPT (= classical trit)   3    2   —
  regular 4-gon GPT (gbit)               2    2   —
  regular 5-gon GPT                      2    2   —
  regular 6-gon GPT                      2    2   —
  regular 7-gon GPT                      2    2   —
  regular 8-gon GPT                      2    2   —
  classical simplex, 2 outcomes          2    1   —
  classical simplex, 3 outcomes          3    2   —
  classical simplex, 4 outcomes          4    3   —
  rebit (real QM, d=2)                   2    2   2 (real)
  qubit (complex QM, d=2)                2    3   2
  spin factor / ball in R^4              2    4   —
  qutrit (complex QM, d=3)               3    8   3
  real QM, d=3                           3    5   3 (real)
  => N = 2 for: classical bit (K=1), rebit (K=2), gbit / polygons (K=2), qubit (K=3), spin factors (K=4, ...):
     SAME CAPACITY != SAME STATE SPACE; capacity does not fix the representation (C4/C5 needs extra principles).

==============================================================================
G4-2 capacity from dynamics
==============================================================================
  Markov chain, 7 states, closed classes {0,1},{2,3},{4} + transients: asymptotic distinguishable outputs = rank(P^inf) = 3 (initial capacity 7)
  collective SU(2) noise on 3 qubits: commutant dim 5, centre dim 2, central blocks 2 with sizes [4, 4], multiplicities m_J = [2, 1] (theory: J=3/2 -> 1, J=1/2 -> 2)
     -> noiseless capacity (perfectly distinguishable after twirl) = sum m_J = 3  (initial 8): CAPACITY DERIVED FROM D (noise symmetry)

==============================================================================
G4-3 access hostile: same state space, restricted effects
==============================================================================
  2 qubits, all effects: N = 4.  Readout restricted to functions of total S_z (collective access):
     N = number of distinct S_z eigenvalues = 3
  qutrit (d = 3), readout restricted to {|0><0|, |1><1| + |2><2|}: N = 2   <- G4 SAME as qubit, G1 (d) DIFFERENT
  qubit, effects restricted to spectrum in [0.1, 0.9] (unsharp access): no effect reaches 0/1 -> N = 1

